    "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo file-backend creators (for example, TP rank 0 in different PP stages) can both observe a missing shared storage directory. The second `os.makedirs` then raises `FileExistsError` during initialization.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUse `exist_ok=True` for directory creation. Keep the existing TP/CP rank guard, path precedence and error propagation unchanged. Add a deterministic CPU regression that pauses both real existence checks before either worker creates the directory, plus existing-directory, nonzero-rank and permission-error controls.\n\n## Tests\n\nLinux, Python 3.12, Torch 2.11.0: 40 tests across the new directory test and the existing file-LRU/path-routing files. The unchanged baseline has 39 passes and one error wrapping the expected race assertion (`FileExistsError`); the final commit passes all 40 with no skips. Exact package/source hashes were checked before and after; no production stubs, installs, model downloads or GPU work. This is component coverage, not an engine-startup or model benchmark.\n\nStandalone Ruff checks/format, isort and the three repository test-registration/entry-point checks passed. File-scoped pre-commit could not fully finish on Windows: its Ruff executable was blocked by application control and three hooks could not find `python3` (those Python checks passed separately). Hosted CI is still needed.\n\n## Accuracy Tests / Speed Tests\n\nNot applicable: no kernel, model-output or steady-state performance change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Full pre-commit / hosted CI\n- [x] Focused registered CPU regression and existing component tests\n- [x] Existing rank and filesystem-error behavior preserved\n- [x] No documentation/API change needed\n\nAI-assisted; the test results above are from independently executed native checks.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38689824667](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38689824667)<!-